# Source-Scoped Question Drafts and Immutable Ask

Status: DONE
Milestone: A1 Local question state
Dependencies: 27_AI_ANSWER_RESEARCH.todo

## Purpose

Choose a dictated or typed question without accidentally sending the rest of a meeting.

## Tasks

- [x] Add a bounded structured transcript store with capture-session/source/segment/epoch/revision identity.
- [x] Preserve existing source-labelled display/export and all prior transcript tests.
- [x] Build an editable local QuestionDraft from explicit selected segments or typed text; armed live-Mic boundaries integrate with29commit.
- [x] Do not infer provenance by parsing rendered `[Mic]` labels or copy the entire transcript.
- [x] Freeze exactly the displayed draft/revision on Ask, including its provisional/final provenance.
- [x] Define empty/oversized input, multi-segment questions, user edits and late ASR revision behavior.
- [x] Keep Computer text out of a Mic draft unless the owner explicitly selects it.
- [x] Add deterministic source/session/revision/cancel/eviction tests with synthetic data.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Only explicit Ask creates a snapshot; no provider is connected in this local slice and natural finals/question marks never auto-send.
- [x] Frozen snapshots are immutable; later transcript text cannot rewrite or resend them.
- [x] Prior unrelated Mic text and all unselected Computer/notes/chat data stay out of the prompt.
- [x] No new recording-permission or recipient-rehearsal confirmation is introduced.

